  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 127 AM EDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nA quiet night so far with only a scattered to broken deck of high \nand mid-level clouds. For the rest of tonight, we should see some \ngradual clearing ahead of additional high clouds moving in around \ndaybreak. Some patchy dense fog development is expected especially \nnear area-waterways. A broad trough begins to dig into the Great \nLakes region today. A weak frontal boundary will move through this \nafternoon, supporting area-wide isolated to scattered storms and \nshowers. SPC SWO does maintain a Marginal (1 out of 5) risk for NE \nTN and SW VA with wind as the primary concern. Forecast soundings \nwould support an isolated damaging wind threat so a Marginal should \nbe sufficient. Additionally, a locally heavy rainfall will also be \npossible.\n\nFor Friday, another weak shortwave will move through the region. \nInstability and moisture will be sufficient to support another day \nof isolated to scattered thunderstorm threat in the afternoon hours. \nForecast soundings show 1500+ J/KG of MLCAPE and modest lapse rates. \nThis should be enough for another isolated severe wind threat Friday \nafternoon. \n\nWe'll begin to gradually warm up as we head into the weekend. \nSaturday's forecast will feature an inverted trough axis across the \neastern half of TN. This should lead to diurnally driven storms \nalong the eastern TN mountains and SW NC. Otherwise, locations west \nof there should have a fairly pleasant and dry day. Sunday into \nearly next will see the return of hot and humid weather across the \nregion. The upper level ridge over the SW CONUS will shift east \nacross the southern tier eventually centering over the SE CONUS by \nmid-week. The combination of rising heights and subsidence under the \nridge will keep the PoPs suppressed, and the forecast mostly dry. \nHowever, high temperatures will trend into the low to mid 90s with \nheat indices in the 100 to 105 range possible for much of the valley \nthrough the end of the forecast period.",
